    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryce Harper** (75.31) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19) headline our lineup as the premier offensive anchors. **Bryce Harper** draws a favorable matchup against Singer, where his elite xwOBA and favorable park factors provide the highest floor in the system. **Taylor Ward** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a platoon edge against Peterson, making him an essential start despite the opponent's decent xERA. We are also capitalizing on the high-upside environment for **Luis Arraez**, **Zack Gelof**, and **Jung Hoo Lee** in their matchup against Ryan Feltner; the combination of favorable wind direction, neutral-to-soft SP delivery, and the premium batting order spots for **Luis Arraez** (#2) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (#5) boosts their efficiency scores well into the \"Strong\" tier.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Masyn Winn**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a score of 39.78\u2014just shy of our 40.0 \"Below Floor\" cutoff. While **Masyn Winn** typically offers the speed profile we crave for this league, he is currently being squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-efficiency platoon advantages elsewhere in the order. His candidacy was further weakened by a brutal matchup against a tough arm (3.03 xERA) and a 38% rain risk that introduces unnecessary volatility. We are proceeding with **Jonathan Aranda** and **JJ Bleday** as our final utility/OF depth despite their lower scores, as they maintain better situational leverage against their respective opponents than **Masyn Winn** does today. Keep a close eye on the \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Luis Arraez**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Drew Gilbert**, and **Jung Hoo Lee**; if these starters drop to the bottom third of the order, their efficiency scores will regress significantly and may require a tactical pivot.",
